    <DataNode elementId="AT5G42810-MONOMER" textLabel="Inositol-pentakisphosphate 2-kinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G42810.1" dataSource="TAIR gene name" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;IPK1&lt;/i&gt; encodes a protein with inositol polyphosphate 2-kinase activity. AtIpk1 was recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; and purified to test its substrate specificity. In the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana atipk1-1&lt;/i&gt; mutants containing a T-DNA insertion in the &lt;i&gt;IPK1&lt;/i&gt; gene, seed phytate (InsP&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt;) levels are reduced by 83% of that of wild-type &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; plants |CITS:[16107538]|. Interestingly, the levels of InsP&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt; precursors (InsP&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; and InsP&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;) increased significantly leading to the production of a total amount of IPs similar to that of wild-type.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G42810-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G42810.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_568613" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="Inositol-1,3,4,5,6-pentakisphosphate 2-kinase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Ins(1,3,4,5,6)P5 2-kinase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="AtIPK1" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="InsP5 2-kinase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-10992, RXN-10991, RXN-10990" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="3" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G42810.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G42810" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16107538" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G07370-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G07370-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LF72" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;IPK2&amp;alpha;&lt;/i&gt; encodes a protein with inositol polyphosphate 6-/3-/5-kinase activity. AtIpk2&amp;alpha; 6-/3-kinase activity is predominant, and this enzyme was shown to convert Ins(1,4,5)P&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; to Ins(1,3,4,5,6)P&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;, predominantly via an Ins(1,4,5,6)P&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; intermediate. This enzyme was also shown to display a novel 5-kinase activity towards Ins(1,3,4,6)P&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; and Ins(1,2,3,4,6)P&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[12226109]|. The protein was recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; and purified to test its substrate specificity. The enzyme was also shown to restore inositol polyphosphate production and the temperature-sensitive growth of &lt;i&gt;ipk2&lt;/i&gt;&amp;Delta; yeast mutant lacking but not that of yeast mutants &lt;i&gt;ipk1&lt;/i&gt;&amp;Delta; or &lt;i&gt;kcs1&lt;/i&gt;&amp;Delta; |CITS:[12226109]|.</Comment>
