    <DataNode elementId="AT5G61760-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G61760-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FLT2" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;IPK2&amp;beta;&lt;/i&gt; encodes a protein with inositol polyphosphate 6-/3-/5-kinase activity. AtIpk2&amp;beta;&apos;s 6-/3-kinase activity is predominant, and this enzyme was shown to convert Ins(1,4,5)P&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; to Ins(1,3,4,5,6)P&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;, predominantly via an Ins(1,4,5,6)P&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; intermediate. This enzyme was also shown to display a novel 5-kinase activity towards Ins(1,3,4,6)P&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; and Ins(1,2,3,4,6)P&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS:[12226109]|. The protein was recombinantly expressed in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; and purified to test its substrate specificity. The enzyme was also shown to restore inositol polyphosphate production and the temperature-sensitive growth of &lt;i&gt;ipk2&lt;/i&gt;&amp;Delta; yeast mutant lacking but not that of yeast mutants &lt;i&gt;ipk1&lt;/i&gt;&amp;Delta; or &lt;i&gt;kcs1&lt;/i&gt;&amp;Delta; |CITS:[12226109]|.</Comment>
